 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. ASN.
* ASSIGN TO a data name (2026-11-22): one SELECT, two
* files, the name chosen at run time.  Expected:
* E1 00 / W1 00 / E2 00 EAST ONE / W2 00 WEST ONE /
* N1 35 / DONE  (W2 opens "west.dat", lower case)
 ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
 INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
 FILE-CONTROL.
     SELECT DB ASSIGN TO WS-NAME
         ORGANIZATION IS RELATIVE
         ACCESS MODE IS DYNAMIC
         RELATIVE KEY IS WS-KEY
         FILE STATUS IS WS-STAT.
 DATA DIVISION.
 FILE SECTION.
 FD  DB.
 01  DB-REC.
     05  DB-TEXT  PIC X(10).
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 77  WS-NAME  PIC X(20) VALUE "EAST.DAT".
 77  WS-KEY   PIC 9(4).
 77  WS-STAT  PIC XX.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION.
 MAIN-PARA.
     OPEN OUTPUT DB.
     MOVE 1 TO WS-KEY.
     MOVE "EAST ONE" TO DB-TEXT.
     WRITE DB-REC.
     DISPLAY "E1 " WS-STAT.
     CLOSE DB.
     MOVE "WEST.DAT" TO WS-NAME.
     OPEN OUTPUT DB.
     MOVE "WEST ONE" TO DB-TEXT.
     WRITE DB-REC.
     DISPLAY "W1 " WS-STAT.
     CLOSE DB.
     MOVE "EAST.DAT" TO WS-NAME.
     OPEN INPUT DB.
     MOVE SPACES TO DB-TEXT.
     READ DB.
     DISPLAY "E2 " WS-STAT " " DB-TEXT.
     CLOSE DB.
     MOVE "west.dat" TO WS-NAME.
     OPEN INPUT DB.
     MOVE SPACES TO DB-TEXT.
     READ DB.
     DISPLAY "W2 " WS-STAT " " DB-TEXT.
     CLOSE DB.
     MOVE "NONE.DAT" TO WS-NAME.
     OPEN INPUT DB.
     DISPLAY "N1 " WS-STAT.
     DISPLAY "DONE".
     STOP RUN.
